    "playerSummary": "BEREGOST — SESSION 1 RECAP: \"Happy Solstice! (...Again!)\"\n\nLOOP 0 — DAWN OF THE SUMMER SOLSTICE (06:00 AM – Afternoon)\n• The Jammed Clocktower (06:00 AM): We started atop Beregost's smashed western Clocktower belfry, pulling a pale bone (and wire) out of the gears so the 6:00 AM bell could chime—only for both to dissolve into dust. Captain Rebecca Thorne thanked us and invited us to the 10:00 AM Solstice Carnival, mentioning two morning errands: smoke to the west and a goblin patrol to the east.\n• Inspecting the Belfry: We roused pajama-clad gnome clockmaker Artificer Bram Copperwheel, who checked three oversized pocket watches and confirmed the clock was running right on time—though the balcony was smashed from an impact, and our CSI investigation mostly turned up scraps of our own gear scattered around the rubble.\n• The West Firebreak (07:00–09:00 AM): Heading 1 hex west into burning farm fields, we spent an hour cutting a firebreak (with owl drone recon confirming the blaze was contained). The grateful farmer rewarded us with 25 gp, and Tobias the Baker gifted a special Warm Loaf (+5 Temp HP & Cold Resistance).\n• The Solstice Carnival (10:00–11:30 AM): Back in town, the day felt unusually warm—\"Lathander's Solstice blessing.\"\n  - Anvil-Ringer: After a rough start with the sledgehammer, Gwen turned into a bear and body-slammed the pressure plate to ring the bell (+1 damage Whetstones—and convincing the dwarf smith she belonged to the northern Druid Grove).\n  - Little Maya's Toy Thrush: Using the owl + well bucket, we fished Maya's wooden bird out of the well. She gifted a Green Clover Bracelet (\"Don't take it off until sundown!\") and whispered a secret: a man by the North Gate had no shadow.\n  - Archery, Rap Battle & Bun-Eating: Won Ribbons of the Morninglord (+1 to a Death Save/fire check) from Sister Althea, a +1d6 Bardic Inspiration token from the bard, and Warm Currant Buns (+2 HP on Short Rest) from Tobias—who mentioned his apprentice went south to the cornfields and hasn't come back.\n• The 11:30 AM Boom & Heat Wipeout: At 11:30 AM, a bone-rattling explosion shook Beregost from the north, knocking the owl off the clocktower. Heading north to investigate, we killed a tentacled Displacer Beast as temperatures spiked to 125°F and then 175°F—forcing us to shoot each other point-blank with an ice bow just to stay cool. We reached a blasted black obsidian crater ringed by wilted brambles before the relentless heat dropped us all on the hike back south. As everything faded, a faint muffled song drifted through the haze...\n\nLOOP 1 — RESET TO 06:00 AM (06:00 AM – 11:25 AM)\n• The Twist: CLACK. GONG. We snapped awake back on the Clocktower balcony at 6:00 AM—full HP, full spell slots, all collected items gone, but every memory intact.\n• The Shadowless Man (07:00 AM): Dispatching the owl to the North Watch Post led us straight to Aurelius—a radiant, finely dressed stranger who cast no shadow (\"It's the solstice—no one's casting a shadow today!\"). He told us a confused Angel is magically tethered to a Devil in the northern Druid Grove, and handed us a golden Crucible Charm to physically attach to the devil's chest to strip its armor.\n• The Druid Grove & Premature Detonation (11:00–11:20 AM): Taking a new northern path through an iron-thorn ravine, we reached the Druids' Grove, intimidated them into letting us advance, and fought off two Displacer Beasts (while Gwen Polymorphed into a Quetzalcoatl to scout from the sky). Ahead, four chanting druids held a massive horned Devil bound in ethereal chains—with no angel in sight. Vaulting the brambles at 11:20 AM, we slapped the Crucible Charm onto the devil's chest... triggering the exact same massive explosion 10 minutes early, instantly vaporizing everyone within 85 feet!\n• Archdruid Faelan's Wrath (11:25 AM): When the survivors pressed the dazed druids for answers and grappled their leader demanding \"one word that will blow your mind an hour ago,\" he snapped—\"When you get to hell, tell them Archdruid Faelan sent you!\"—transformed into a giant bear, and flattened the rest of the party.\n\nNEXT SESSION (START OF LOOP 2 — 06:00 AM):\nBack atop the Clocktower balcony at 6:00 AM with full health, full spells, and a growing list of leads: Aurelius at the North Gate (we want to interrogate him!), what really happened at the Druid Grove, the missing baker's apprentice to the south, the goblin patrol to the east, and why the world turns lethally hot after midday.",
